# .globals/sets: the one always-on policy file.
# Row: `name  token...`. Tokens: main, lane, !mac, !linux, only:<harness>, not:<harness>.
# `lane` implies `main` and is written as both. Edit with `skillherd on|off`, or by hand;
# `skillherd render` applies it.
#
# Keep this list SHORT. Every always-on skill puts its name and description in every
# session's context, and bulk always-on lists degrade into noise: the list this was
# modelled on grew from 20 to 80+ entries three times and had to be cut back each time.
# Everything else stays dormant in the pool: find it with `skillherd search`, switch it on
# for one project with `skillherd add <name>` (or `skillherd add @dev`), or globally with
# `skillherd on <name>` when it has earned a place here.

# build discipline
task-design            main lane
no-ceremony            main lane
debugging-systematic   main
tdd                    main
grilling               main
